        "title": "Equivalent fractions general rule",
        "text": "Recall that two fractions are equivalent if $$\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{ca}{cb}$$ for some nonzero number c. If multiplying the fraction by $$\\frac{2x}{4x^2+\\frac{1}{4}}$$, this number must be $$1$$",
